= Former Supreme Chancellor Finis Valorum

Brought down by the Naboo crisis, Valorum has had time to think about who arranged his fall. He is disgraced, but not a fool.

[? if advisor_action_timer > 0 : *Our advisors can act again in [+ advisor_action_timer +] turn(s).* ?]

- @valorum_networks: Old Chancellery networks.
- @valorum_elder: Elder statesman.
- @valorum_bureaucracy: Call in favours from the civil service.
- @go_back: Back.

@valorum_networks
subtitle: +1 evidence (less each time).
choose-if: advisor_action_timer <= 0
unavailable-subtitle: Our advisors have already acted recently.
on-arrival: evidence += 1 / (1 + valorum_leads); valorum_leads += 1; advisor_action_timer = 5

Valorum still has friends in the Chancellery’s offices. They remember which visitors came to the Naboo delegation late at night.

@valorum_elder
subtitle: +6 relations with the Core Moderates.
choose-if: advisor_action_timer <= 0
unavailable-subtitle: Our advisors have already acted recently.
on-arrival: mod_relation += 6; advisor_action_timer = 5

The Core Moderates still remember Valorum’s better days. He reminds them that the Caucus kept faith with him.

@valorum_bureaucracy
subtitle: Warms the Senate bureaucracy towards us considerably; −1 corruption.
choose-if: advisor_action_timer <= 0
unavailable-subtitle: Our advisors have already acted recently.
on-arrival: bureau_relation += 15; corruption -= 1; advisor_action_timer = 5

Valorum ran the Senate's machinery for years. He knows which clerks owe him favours, which committee secretaries he promoted, and which audits were never finished. He calls the favours in.
